==Premise==
Six teenagers from different backgrounds unite against a common enemy – their criminal parents,<ref name="RunawaysHulu" /> who collectively run an organization called [[Pride (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Pride]].<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /> In the second season, the teenagers are now on the run from their parents, living on their own and figuring out how to stop Pride.<ref name="Topher" /> The third season sees [[Nico Minoru]] and the other members of the team face off against aliens and [[Morgan le Fay (Marvel Comics)|Morgan le Fay]].<ref name="S3PremiereDate" />

==Cast and characters==
===Main===
* {{anchor|Alex Wilder}}[[Rhenzy Feliz]] as [[Alex Wilder (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Alex Wilder]]: A nerd who longs to reunite with his childhood friends. He has a high intellect and is the leader of the Runaways.<ref name="CastAnnounce" /> 
* {{anchor|Nico Minoru}}[[Lyrica Okano]] as [[Nico Minoru (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Nico Minoru]]: <br />A [[Wicca]]n who isolates herself with her [[Gothic fashion|gothic]] appearance and is a member of the Runaways.<ref name="CastAnnounce" /> Unlike the comics, Nico does not summon the [[Staff of One]] through [[self-harm]]. Okano said this was tweaked, "for good reason" as there would be "a lot of young teenagers watching the show and we don't want to promote anything like self-harm because that's serious". She added that an element of drawing blood would still be involved.<ref name="StaffOfOneSelfHarm" />
* {{anchor|Karolina Dean}}[[Virginia Gardner]] as [[Karolina Dean (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Karolina Dean]]: <br />A human-alien hybrid burdened by her religious upbringing who wants to pursue her own desires instead of following in her mother's footsteps, and is a member of the Runaways.<ref name="CastAnnounce" /> Karolina has the ability of flight, to glow with rainbow-colored light, and to shoot beams of light.<ref name="KarolinaLight" />
* {{anchor|Gertrude Yorkes}}[[Ariela Barer]] as [[Gertrude Yorkes (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Gertrude Yorkes]]: A [[riot grrrl]], social activist, and a member of the Runaways. She also has a telepathic link with her genetically engineered dinosaur, Old Lace.<ref name="CastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Chase Stein}}[[Gregg Sulkin]] as [[Chase Stein (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Chase Stein]]: <br />A high school lacrosse player who is often dismissed as a dumb jock, but displays brilliance in engineering and is a member of the Runaways.<ref name="CastAnnounce" /> Sulkin and the writers wanted the character to be "more layered" than the comics, and Sulkin felt that Chase was the most changed of the Runaways from the source material.<ref name="SulkinWizard" /> The character is depicted as having the potential to be as much of a genius as his father is,<ref name="MarstersInspiration" /> and builds gadgets, including powerful weaponized gauntlets called "Fistigons".<ref name="ChaseBuildsGadgets" /> Connor Falk portrays a young Chase.<ref name="Ep7" />
* {{anchor|Molly Hernandez}}Allegra Acosta as [[Molly Hayes Hernandez]]:<br />The youngest member of the Runaways who is characterized by her positive attitude. Molly discovers she has the ability of superhuman strength and invulnerability.<ref name="CastAnnounce" /> Evelyn Angelos portrays a young Molly.<ref name="Ep3" />
* {{anchor|Catherine Wilder}}[[Angel Parker]] as [[Catherine Wilder (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Catherine Wilder]]: Alex's mother, a successful lawyer, and a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Geoffrey Wilder}}[[Ryan Sands]] as [[Geoffrey Wilder (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Geoffrey Wilder]]: Alex's father and a self-made business man who had a grueling path to his success and is a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Leslie Dean}}[[Annie Wersching]] as [[Leslie Dean (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Leslie Dean]] ({{nee}} Ellerh):<br />Karolina's mother, one of the leaders of the cult-like religious group the Church of [[Gibborim (comics)|Gibborim]] and a member of the Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /><ref name="Deans" /> Mia Topalian portrays a young Leslie Ellerh, while Charlie Townsend portrays her as a toddler.
* {{anchor|Frank Dean}}[[Kip Pardue]] as [[Frank Dean (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Frank Dean]]: <br />Karolina's father, a former teen star who is struggling in his professional acting career and becomes one of the leaders of the Church of Gibborim.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /><ref name="Deans" /> Unlike the comics, Frank is not currently a member of Pride. Pardue described the character as the "liaison" between the Runaways and Pride, saying, "This whole show is about the kids fighting their parents. Frank toes that line and has to find out where his allegiances lie".<ref name="PardueEW" />
* {{anchor|Janet Stein}}[[Ever Carradine]] as [[Janet Stein (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Janet Stein]]: Chase's mother who has a brilliant mind, is "a perfect [[Parent-Teacher Association|PTA]] mom", and a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /> [[Sorel Carradine]] (Ever's cousin) portrays a young Janet.<ref name="Ep7" />
* {{anchor|Victor Stein}}[[James Marsters]] as [[Victor Stein (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Victor Stein]]: <br />Chase's father, an engineering genius and a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /> Marsters was inspired by [[Vincent D'Onofrio]]'s portrayal of [[Kingpin (character)|Wilson Fisk]] in ''[[Daredevil (TV series)|Daredevil]]'', saying it was "exactly opposite of what I was expecting", and also looked for common ground with Victor, saying, "I'm not an abusive parent but I'm not a perfect parent. I don't think anyone is." He added that Victor just wants Chase to live up to his potential.<ref name="MarstersInspiration" /> [[Tim Pocock]] portrays a young Victor.<ref name="Ep7" /> 
* {{anchor|Stacey Yorkes}}[[Brigid Brannagh]] as [[Stacey Yorkes (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Stacey Yorkes]]: Gert's mother, a bioengineer, and a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Dale Yorkes}}[[Kevin Weisman]] as [[Dale Yorkes (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Dale Yorkes]]: Gert's father, a bioengineer, and a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Tina Minoru}}[[Brittany Ishibashi]] as [[Tina Minoru (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tina Minoru]]: <br />Nico's mother who is a brilliant innovator, ruthless CEO, and perfectionist "[[Tiger mother|tiger mom]]" who is a member of Pride.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" /> The character previously appeared in the film ''[[Doctor Strange (2016 film)|Doctor Strange]]'', in a minor role as a Master of the Mystic Arts, portrayed by [[Linda Louise Duan]].<ref name="DSPrelude" /><ref name="AnnouncementCB" /><ref name="Duan" /> The producers felt free to recast the role and create a different version of Tina Minoru since Duan was not named as the character in the film.<ref name="ShowrunnersIGNAug2017" />
* {{anchor|Robert Minoru}}[[James Yaegashi]] as [[Robert Minoru (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Robert Minoru]]: Nico's father and a member of Pride who is a brilliant innovator.<ref name="PrideCastAnnounce" />
* {{anchor|Jonah}}[[Julian McMahon]] as Jonah: <br />Karolina's biological father, a member of the alien race known as the Gibborim who is the Pride's benefactor.<ref name="McMahonCast" /> McMahon described Jonah as "the wealthy guy who's pretty ego-driven and mission-driven... who's trying to accomplish certain things and if something were to get in his way he'd plow through it", which he felt was similar to [[Doctor Doom|Victor von Doom]], whom he portrayed in ''[[Fantastic Four (2005 film)|Fantastic Four]]'' and [[Fantastic Four: Rise of the Silver Surfer|its sequel]]. He also revealed that he did not appear in the earlier episodes as the character in his near-death state, as he had been cast after the first four episodes had been completed.<ref name="McMahonIGN" /> Ric Sarabia portrayed the character in this state,<ref name="Sarabia" /> which McMahon stated took five hours of make up application to achieve.<ref name="McMahonIGN" /><!-- 101, 102, 103, 104, 105 (Sarabia credit as mysterious man) / 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110 (McMahon credit) -->
* {{anchor|Xavin}}Clarissa Thibeaux as [[Xavin (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Xavin]]: A shape-shifting alien who believes in a prophecy that they are betrothed to Karolina. <!-- 209, 211, 212, 213 -->

